Mungerʼs latticework of mental models enabled holistic analysis:
Key Models from Mathematics:
Compound Interest:
Munger emphasized that “the first rule of compounding: Never interrupt it unnecessarily” .
A $10M investment growing at 18% annually becomes $754M in 40 years .
Discounted Cash Flow:
He prioritized DCF over relative valuation metrics, noting “all intelligent investing is value
investing” .
Psychological Models:
Inversion Principle: Assessing how businesses could fail before evaluating upside
Circle of Competence: Restricting investments to understandable industries
Confirmation Bias Mitigation: Actively seeking disconfirming evidence
Mungerʼs final portfolio held just 4 equities while generating $2.2B net worth :
Holding Position Size Holding Period CAGR
Wells Fargo $65M 19902023 9.2%
Costco $167M 19972023 14.7%
Bank of America $63M 20112023 6.8%
Alibaba $26M 20212023 18%
Source: SEC 13F Filings
This concentration produced volatility 53% drawdown in 197374 ) but ultimately
outperformed through selective bets on compounders.
