Munger identified critical behavioral traps:
Common Biases vs. Mungerʼs Antidotes
Bias Example Mungerʼs Solution
Recency Bias Chasing tech bubbles Focus on 10-year trends
Loss Aversion Selling compounders in dips “Be fearful when others are greedy”
Overconfidence Trading frequency Stay within circle of competence
He institutionalized checklists to counter these tendencies, including:
Is the business model understandable?
Does management allocate capital rationally?
Does the company generate owner earnings?
Is the price 90% of intrinsic value?
On Valuation:
“All intelligent investing is value investing – acquiring more than you pay for. You
must value the business to value the stock.”
On Patience:
“The big money is not in the buying and selling, but in the waiting.”
On Risk Management:
“If youʼre not willing to react with equanimity to a 50% decline, you shouldnʼt own
stocks.”
