2. Implementation Guide

Conservative growth assumptions (≤ GDP + inflation)
Scenario analysis with margin of safety thresholds
Step 3 Implement position sizing rules:
Maximum 5% per initial position
Increase to 25%+ only after 3+ years of thesis validation
Mungerʼs legacy demonstrates that concentrated quality investing can outperform despite
short-term volatility. For modern investors, key adaptations include:
Applying machine learning to identify durable moats in tech-driven markets
Developing dynamic DCF models that adjust discount rates for macro regimes
Building behavioral nudges to maintain discipline during drawdowns
As Munger observed: “Itʼs not supposed to be easy. Anyone who finds it easy is stupid.” By
combining his multidisciplinary framework with rigorous financial modeling, investors can
systematically improve decision-making – even in increasingly complex markets.
“The world is full of foolish gamblers. Theyʼll do worse than the patient investors.” – Charlie
Munger
